# Fasting: "If you would begin your draw step, you may skip that step instead. If you do, you gain 2 life" (CR 614.10,
# 500.11), and "at the beginning of your upkeep, put a hunger counter on this enchantment. Then destroy this enchantment
# if it has five or more hunger counters on it." Bot1 casts it on turn 1 and skips each of its draw steps after: each skip
# gains exactly 2 life and draws nothing, so Fasting's own "when you draw a card" never destroys it, and Bot2's draws
# (each of its turns) don't either - only "you" drawing does. The counter goes on before the count is read (the ruling):
# at four counters (turn 9) Fasting stays; the fifth, on turn 11, destroys it in the upkeep, so Bot1 draws that turn.
# Fasting {W}: Enchantment
#   At the beginning of your upkeep, put a hunger counter on this enchantment. Then destroy this enchantment if it has five or more hunger counters on it.
#   If you would begin your draw step, you may skip that step instead. If you do, you gain 2 life.
#   When you draw a card, destroy this enchantment.

